{title: 'Tis So Sweet to Trust in Jesus}
{artist: Louisa M. R. Stead}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune TRUST IN JESUS - William J. Kirkpatrick (1882)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1882, tune 1882: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
'Tis so [G]sweet to trust in Jesus, just to [D]take Him at His word;
Just to [G]rest upon His promise, just to [D]know, "Thus saith the [G]Lord."
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Jesus, Jesus, how I [C]trust Him! How I've [G]proved Him o'er and [D]o'er!
[G]Jesus, Jesus, precious [C]Jesus! O for [G]grace to [D]trust Him [G]more!
{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
O how [G]sweet to trust in Jesus, just to [D]trust His cleansing blood;
Just in [G]simple faith to plunge me 'neath the [D]healing, cleansing [G]flood!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I'm so [G]glad I learned to trust Thee, precious [D]Jesus, Savior, Friend;
And I [G]know that Thou art with me, wilt be [D]with me to the [G]end.
{end_of_verse}
